.TH HL 1
.SH NAME
hl \- tree-sitter's colors in acme's windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hl
[
.B -s
.I astyles
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Hl
colors the text of
.IR acme (1)'s
windows by its syntax, as tree-sitter's grammars parse it,
in each window's
.IR astyles (4)
layer
.BR treesitter .
It waits for
.BR $acmesrv ,
an acme's
.B /srv
file, and follows its windows, mounted on
.BR /mnt/acme ,
through
.IR amux (4)
sessions when
.B /mnt/amux
has them (see
.IR acme (2)),
writing their layers in
.I astyles
.RB ( /mnt/astyles ).
.PP
.I Hl
runs one
.IR syn ,
the syntax programs' router (see
.IR syn (4)),
and names each window to it by the window's file;
a window whose file the first rule of
.B $home/lib/syn
or
.B /lib/syn
matches is colored by that rule's language.
.I Hl
gives
.I syn
a window's body once, under acme's
.B seq
guard, and then its edits, from the window's
.BR rdevent ,
and writes in its layer only the runs that
.I syn
says may have changed since the edit as of which it last wrote the layer,
each under the
.B seq
of the edits it reflects, so that
.I astyles
refuses colors for text that has since changed,
and
.I hl
colors that text again from that same edit after the next edits.
A Get, an edit whose text
.B rdevent
leaves out, or a program that has lost the document
has
.I hl
give the body again.
A span answered
.B lost
or
.B "program gone"
has
.I hl
give the body again too, and one answered
.B stale
has it ask for the window's runs whole, by
.BR "span" " id " - .
.I Hl
gives up on
.I syn
only when its answers end, and then runs it again.
A window whose program cannot start, whose body
.I syn
does not answer with runs, whose span it answers with another error, or whose language a
.I syn
run again does not know, is left as it is until a Get or Put, when
.I hl
names it to
.I syn
again.
.I Syn
gives a fenced block of code in a markdown file to the program of the rule with the block's
name among its
.BR fence= ,
so a block marked
.B sh
is colored as
.BR bash .
.PP
.I Hl
sends
.I syn
the requests
.BR lang ,
.BR body ,
.BR insert ,
.BR delete ,
.B span
and
.B close
of
.IR syn (4).
A program's queries, in
.BR /sys/lib/ts ,
say what its runs are, and
.B /sys/lib/ts/names
the
.IR theme (6)
name each run takes.
.SH FILES
.TF /sys/lib/ts/names
.TP
.B /lib/syn
the languages' rules
.TP
.B /sys/lib/ts/names
capture names to
.IR theme (6)
names
.TP
.B /bin/syn
the router
.TP
.BI /bin/ts/ lang
a language's program
.PD
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B src/cmd/hl.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR acme (1),
.IR Tree (1),
.IR acme (2),
.IR amux (4),
.IR astyles (4),
.IR syn (4),
.IR theme (6)
